<div class="modal fade" id="notebook-help-modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="notebook-help-title" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable modal-fullscreen-sm-down">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h2 class="modal-title fs-5" id="notebook-help-title">Taking notes</h2>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close help"></button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold">Start a note</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Sign in and connect your Google Drive from <a href="<%= utils.urlFor(req, '/settings') %>">My Settings</a>. Your notes are saved as Markdown files in your own Drive.</li>
          <li>Select <strong>New note</strong> in My Notebook to create a general note, or select the <i class="bi bi-sticky" aria-hidden="true"></i> note icon beside a hadith, Quran ayah, or tafsir.</li>
          <li>Give the note a title that is different from your other note titles, then write your note. Changes save automatically after you pause typing; use the checkmark to save and preview.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Use the eye/pencil control to switch between preview and editing. Click the title or tags to edit them; they collapse when you return to the note body. Add tags separated by spaces, or write hashtags such as <code>#reflection</code> in your note. Use search and tag filters to find notes later.</p>
        <p>The <strong>notes created</strong> count under My Notebook is your lifetime total. A note counts after its first successful save. Editing, autosaving, and sharing do not add to it, and deleting a note does not reduce it. Existing saved notes are included where their file records are still available; notes permanently removed before counting began may not be recoverable.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Keep a note open while reading</h3>
        <p>Select the pin icon in a note's header to float it beside the page. The minus icon minimizes it to a <strong>Restore note</strong> button. You can scroll and browse the site while it stays available; the saved note reopens as you move between pages in the same tab. Select the pin again to return to the regular dialog, or close the note to stop following it.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Read and edit in fullscreen</h3>
        <p>Select the <i class="bi bi-arrows-fullscreen" aria-hidden="true"></i> <strong>Expand note</strong> button in the header to fill the screen. Select <strong>Restore note size</strong> to return to the smaller view.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Recent notes:</strong> The left sidebar lists your notes by most recent modification. Select a note to switch to it, or select <strong>New note</strong> to start a blank note. Current edits save before you switch.</li>
          <li><strong>Sidebar controls:</strong> Use the arrow on either sidebar to collapse or expand it. Drag its inner edge to change its width on wider screens, or focus the edge and use the left and right arrow keys. Your sidebar layout is remembered in this browser.</li>
          <li><strong>Heading outline:</strong> In preview, headings from <code>#</code> through <code>######</code> appear under <strong>On this note</strong>. Select a heading to jump to that section. The outline stays visible as you scroll and highlights your current section. It sits beside the note on wider screens and above it on narrow screens. It is hidden while editing or when the note has no headings.</li>
          <li><strong>Text size:</strong> Use the slider at the bottom to shrink or enlarge the note from <strong>75% to 200%</strong>. It works in both preview and editing; <strong>100%</strong> is the default size. This changes your fullscreen view without changing the saved Markdown or printed text size.</li>
        </ul>

        <%- include('markdown_help_content.ejs'); %>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Keyboard shortcuts</h3>
        <p>While editing a note, select the text you want to format, then use a shortcut below. Use <kbd>Cmd</kbd> on Mac or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> on Windows and Linux. These work in the regular, floating, and fullscreen editors.</p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Formatting</th><th scope="col">Shortcut</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Bold</th><td><kbd>Cmd/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>B</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Italic</th><td><kbd>Cmd/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>I</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Underline / Arabic overline</th><td><kbd>Cmd/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>U</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Highlight</th><td><kbd>Cmd/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>H</kbd></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Strikethrough</th><td><kbd>Cmd/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>X</kbd></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>The shortcut adds Markdown markers and keeps your text selected. Press the same shortcut again to remove that formatting, or use another shortcut to combine styles. Arabic and English both work. Changes save automatically; switch to preview to see the result. Select text first: these formatting shortcuts do nothing at an empty cursor. Use <kbd>Cmd/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Z</kbd> to undo, and <kbd>Cmd/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Enter</kbd> to return to preview.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Link your notes</h3>
        <p>Type <code>[[</code> followed by at least two letters from a note title to see suggestions. Matching ignores case and diacritics and can find words anywhere in a title.</p>
        <p><code>[[The Mahdi]]</code> links to that note. Use <code>[[The Mahdi|my research]]</code> to display a different label. Note links and ordinary web links open in a new tab.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Expand a reference</h3>
        <p>Type a plain reference such as <code>bukhari:1</code>, <code>quran:1:1</code>, or <code>quran:17:18-20</code>. Put the reference on a line of its own and press Enter to expand it in place while editing. In preview, you can also select its <i class="bi bi-arrows-angle-expand" aria-hidden="true"></i> expand icon to replace it with the Arabic text, English translation, and source citation. Quran ranges include each ayah in order. Ayahs use ﴿ ﴾ and hadiths use « »; each language ends with its source citation.</p>
        <p>The expand icon is not shown for references inside an explicit Markdown link or code.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Share a read-only note</h3>
        <p>Select the <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up" aria-hidden="true"></i> <strong>Share note</strong> button in the top toolbar, then <strong>Create public link</strong>. Your latest edits are saved before the link is created. Use <strong>Copy link</strong> to share it, or <strong>Open link</strong> to check the public view.</p>
        <p>Anyone with the link can see your name and profile image and read the note’s title and latest saved text without signing in. Readers cannot edit the note. Your email, tags, other notes, and private Google Drive file are not shared. Links to other private notes appear as text. Future saved edits appear at the same public link.</p>
        <p>Shared notes with headings include an <strong>On this note</strong> outline. Readers can select a heading to jump to its section; the outline highlights the current section while scrolling and stays beside the note on desktop and above it on mobile. The <strong>Text size</strong> slider adjusts reading size from 75% to 200% without changing the saved note.</p>
        <p>Select <strong>Stop sharing</strong> to revoke the link. Sharing again creates a new link. Deleting the note or disconnecting Google Drive makes the public note unavailable. Revoking a link cannot remove copies a reader has already saved.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Download your notes</h3>
        <p>The download icon inside a note saves that note as a Markdown file. The download icon on My Notebook saves your notebook as a ZIP file.</p>
        <p class="mb-0">Select the printer icon in a note’s top toolbar to print its formatted text, title, source, and tags, including your latest edits. Choose <strong>Save as PDF</strong> in the print dialog to download a PDF, or select your printer for a paper copy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Got it</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
